Physical options
- A wall calendar with notes section for gifts and reminders.
- A small dedicated planner/notebook (monthly spreads) where you track people and gift ideas.

Automations & imports
- Import birthdays from your phone contacts into Google Calendar (Settings > Import or use the “Birthdays” calendar).
- Export a CSV from a spreadsheet of names/dates and import to Google Calendar if you have a long list.

Maintenance tips
- Set two reminders: one “planning” reminder (2 weeks) and one “wrap/ship” reminder (2 days).
- Review the calendar monthly; update gift ideas or addresses as needed.
- After an event, mark it done and jot down what you gave (handy next year).
- Keep a shared document (Google Doc) for big family gift planning or group cards.

Privacy & etiquette
- Avoid storing sensitive info (full addresses, credit card details) in calendars; use a secure notes app or password manager for those details.
- If you share the calendar, only share with people you trust.

